            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chainless-ftr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chainless foundation treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " blanket is 75 x 90 cm. The first row is worked as chainless foundation stitches, each one simultaneously creating a treble and its own foundation chain below. After the foundation row the blanket continues in plain treble."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chainless foundation gives a stretchier, neater bottom edge than a chain start. DK cotton shows the edge difference clearly. Total yardage is around 360 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "360 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to work chainless foundation treble"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 4 (counts as setup). Yarn over. Insert hook into the 4th ch from hook. Pull up loop. Yarn over, draw through 1 loop (this makes the foundation chain stitch below). Yarn over, draw through 2. Yarn over, draw through 2. One foundation treble made and one chain base created. For each subsequent ftr: yarn over, insert hook into the chain base of the last stitch (the bottom loop), pull up loop, and complete the treble."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 tr x 8 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. The foundation row gauge matches the body row gauge when the foundation stitches are worked at the same tension."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain (setup only)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ftr: chainless foundation treble (row 1 only)"
